  "name": "Haam seui go (Tanka salt-water songs of the Pearl River Delta)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Songs of the Tanka boat-dwelling fishing communities of the Pearl River Delta and the Hong Kong coast, sung in Cantonese without accompaniment, solo or traded between two or more singers, for courtship, at weddings and funerals, and in daily life afloat; passed on orally, they were seldom written down. The Zhongshan form (xianshui ge) is listed on China's national intangible-heritage register, and salt-water songs are on Hong Kong's intangible cultural heritage inventory under the performing arts.",
